---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---
<SiteLayout title="Account" description="Your trusted Hara World session and Git-reviewed community profile.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Community identity / trusted handoff</p>
      <h1>Your Hara World account.</h1>
      <p class="lede">GitHub sign-in remains centralized at Hara Identity. World exchanges a short-lived, PKCE-bound code for its own host-only session before it accepts a profile proposal.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="shell account-stack">
      <article class="account-panel">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Central identity</p>
            <h2 data-world-account-title>Checking Identity…</h2>
          </div>
          <p data-world-account-copy>The shared account control is reading the central GitHub-backed Hara session.</p>
        </div>
        <dl class="definition-list" data-world-account-details hidden>
          <dt>Provider</dt><dd>GitHub through <code>id.hara-lang.org</code></dd>
          <dt>Stable subject</dt><dd data-world-account-id>—</dd>
          <dt>Current login</dt><dd data-world-account-login>—</dd>
          <dt>Authority</dt><dd>Human identity only. Package, specification, repository, and editorial grants remain separate.</dd>
        </dl>
      </article>

      <article class="account-panel">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">World session</p>
            <h2 data-world-session-title>Checking World…</h2>
          </div>
          <p data-world-session-copy>World is checking for its audience-bound local session.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button" href="/api/auth/start?returnTo=/me" data-world-authorize hidden>Enable profile editing</a>
          <button class="button button--quiet" type="button" data-world-logout hidden>End World session</button>
        </div>
        <p class="form-status" data-world-session-status aria-live="polite"></p>
      </article>

      <article class="account-panel" data-profile-editor hidden>
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Git-reviewed profile</p>
            <h2>Propose your public profile.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Your stable GitHub ID, current login, reviewed roles, and existing verified links are supplied server-side. The form cannot override them.</p>
        </div>

        <form class="profile-form" data-profile-form>
          <label>
            <span>Public profile slug</span>
            <input name="slug" required maxlength="64" pattern="[a-z0-9](?:[a-z0-9-]{0,62}[a-z0-9])?" autocomplete="off" />
            <small>The slug becomes fixed after the first profile is merged.</small>
          </label>
          <label>
            <span>Display name</span>
            <input name="displayName" required maxlength="100" autocomplete="name" />
          </label>
          <label class="profile-form__wide">
            <span>Summary</span>
            <textarea name="summary" required maxlength="320" rows="3"></textarea>
          </label>
          <label>
            <span>Location</span>
            <input name="location" maxlength="100" autocomplete="address-level2" />
          </label>
          <label>
            <span>Website</span>
            <input name="website" type="url" inputmode="url" placeholder="https://…" maxlength="300" />
          </label>
          <label class="profile-form__wide">
            <span>Interests</span>
            <input name="interests" maxlength="500" placeholder="Hara, runtimes, programmable media" />
            <small>Comma-separated; at most twelve entries.</small>
          </label>
          <label class="profile-form__wide">
            <span>Biography</span>
            <textarea name="bio" required maxlength="5000" rows="10"></textarea>
          </label>
          <label class="profile-form__wide profile-consent">
            <input name="consent" type="checkbox" required />
            <span>I understand that the proposed profile is public, stored in Git history, and published only after review and merge.</span>
          </label>
          <div class="profile-form__wide hero-actions">
            <button class="button" type="submit" data-profile-submit>Open draft profile PR</button>
            <a class="text-link" href="/people">View the contributor directory</a>
          </div>
          <p class="profile-form__wide form-status" data-profile-status aria-live="polite"></p>
        </form>
      </article>

      <div class="policy-grid account-boundaries">
        <article class="policy-card">
          <h3>One-time exchange</h3>
          <p>The browser carries only a short-lived authorization code bound to a PKCE verifier. World exchanges it directly with Identity.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="policy-card">
          <h3>Separate session key</h3>
          <p>World signs its own two-hour host-only cookie. It never receives the central Identity session-signing secret.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="policy-card">
          <h3>Git remains management</h3>
          <p>Profile edits create draft pull requests through a narrowly scoped GitHub App. Merge remains the publication event.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="policy-card">
          <h3>Consent remains separate</h3>
          <p>A GitHub identity is not automatically linked to a newsletter email or to package-publishing authority.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script>
    const accountTitle = document.querySelector("[data-world-account-title]");
    const accountCopy = document.querySelector("[data-world-account-copy]");
    const accountDetails = document.querySelector("[data-world-account-details]");
    const accountId = document.querySelector("[data-world-account-id]");
    const accountLogin = document.querySelector("[data-world-account-login]");
    const sessionTitle = document.querySelector("[data-world-session-title]");
    const sessionCopy = document.querySelector("[data-world-session-copy]");
    const sessionStatus = document.querySelector("[data-world-session-status]");
    const authorize = document.querySelector("[data-world-authorize]");
    const logout = document.querySelector("[data-world-logout]");
    const editor = document.querySelector("[data-profile-editor]");
    const form = document.querySelector("[data-profile-form]");
    const profileStatus = document.querySelector("[data-profile-status]");
    const submit = document.querySelector("[data-profile-submit]");

    const renderCentral = (session) => {
      const profile = session?.profile || session?.user;
      const signedIn = Boolean(session?.authenticated && profile?.id && profile?.login);
      if (!accountTitle || !accountCopy || !accountDetails || !accountId || !accountLogin) return;
      if (signedIn) {
        accountTitle.textContent = `Signed in as @${profile.login}`;
        accountCopy.textContent = "This central identity can be handed to World without exposing the GitHub provider token or central session key.";
        accountId.textContent = `github:${profile.id}`;
        accountLogin.textContent = `@${profile.login}`;
        accountDetails.hidden = false;
      } else {
        accountTitle.textContent = session?.configured === false ? "GitHub sign-in is not configured" : "Not signed in";
        accountCopy.textContent = session?.configured === false
          ? "The central Identity deployment is reachable, but OAuth or its session secret is not configured."
          : "Use the Sign in control in the header, then establish a World session below.";
        accountDetails.hidden = true;
      }
    };

    const loadProfile = async () => {
      if (!form || !profileStatus) return;
      const response = await fetch("/api/profile", { credentials: "include", headers: { Accept: "application/json" }, cache: "no-store" });
      const body = await response.json().catch(() => ({}));
      if (!response.ok) throw new Error(body?.error?.message || "The profile registry could not be loaded.");
      const profile = body.profile;
      for (const name of ["slug", "displayName", "summary", "location", "website", "bio"]) {
        const field = form.elements.namedItem(name);
        if (field) field.value = profile?.[name] ?? "";
      }
      const interests = form.elements.namedItem("interests");
      if (interests) interests.value = Array.isArray(profile?.interests) ? profile.interests.join(", ") : "";
      const slug = form.elements.namedItem("slug");
      if (slug) slug.readOnly = Boolean(profile?.exists);
      profileStatus.textContent = profile?.exists
        ? `Editing the Git-reviewed profile at ${profile.path}. Reviewed roles are preserved.`
        : "No public profile exists yet. Submitting will create a draft pull request.";
    };

    const renderWorld = async (session) => {
      const signedIn = Boolean(session?.authenticated && session?.profile?.id);
      if (!sessionTitle || !sessionCopy || !authorize || !logout || !editor || !sessionStatus) return;
      authorize.hidden = signedIn || session?.configured === false;
      logout.hidden = !signedIn;
      editor.hidden = !signedIn;
      if (signedIn) {
        sessionTitle.textContent = `World session active for @${session.profile.login}`;
        sessionCopy.textContent = `Host-only World access expires at ${new Date(session.profile.expiresAt).toLocaleString()}.`;
        sessionStatus.textContent = "Profile proposals are now authorized by the server-verified GitHub identity.";
        await loadProfile().catch((error) => { if (profileStatus) profileStatus.textContent = error.message; });
      } else {
        sessionTitle.textContent = session?.configured === false ? "World handoff is not configured" : "No World session";
        sessionCopy.textContent = session?.configured === false
          ? "World still needs its handoff, session, and GitHub App deployment secrets."
          : "Enable profile editing to exchange the central identity for a local World session.";
        sessionStatus.textContent = "The central header identity alone cannot authorize World writes.";
      }
    };

    const refreshWorld = async () => {
      const response = await fetch("/api/auth/session", { credentials: "include", headers: { Accept: "application/json" }, cache: "no-store" });
      const body = await response.json().catch(() => ({ authenticated: false, configured: false }));
      await renderWorld(body);
      return body;
    };

    addEventListener("hara:identity-change", (event) => renderCentral(event.detail));
    logout?.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      logout.disabled = true;
      await fetch("/api/auth/logout", {
        method: "POST",
        credentials: "include",
        headers: { "X-Hara-Request": "world-sign-out" },
      }).catch(() => {});
      await refreshWorld();
      logout.disabled = false;
    });

    form?.addEventListener("submit", async (event) => {
      event.preventDefault();
      if (!profileStatus || !submit) return;
      submit.disabled = true;
      profileStatus.textContent = "Preparing a Git-reviewed profile proposal…";
      const data = new FormData(form);
      const payload = {
        slug: data.get("slug"),
        displayName: data.get("displayName"),
        summary: data.get("summary"),
        location: data.get("location"),
        website: data.get("website"),
        interests: String(data.get("interests") || "").split(","),
        bio: data.get("bio"),
        consent: data.get("consent") === "on",
      };
      try {
        const response = await fetch("/api/profile", {
          method: "POST",
          credentials: "include",
          headers: {
            Accept: "application/json",
            "Content-Type": "application/json",
            "X-Hara-Request": "profile-proposal",
          },
          body: JSON.stringify(payload),
        });
        const body = await response.json().catch(() => ({}));
        if (!response.ok) throw new Error(body?.error?.message || "The profile proposal could not be created.");
        if (body.unchanged) {
          profileStatus.textContent = "The profile already matches the reviewed Git record; no pull request was needed.";
        } else {
          profileStatus.innerHTML = "Draft pull request created: ";
          const link = document.createElement("a");
          link.href = body.pullRequestUrl;
          link.target = "_blank";
          link.rel = "noopener noreferrer";
          link.textContent = `#${body.number}`;
          profileStatus.append(link);
        }
      } catch (error) {
        profileStatus.textContent = error.message;
      } finally {
        submit.disabled = false;
      }
    });

    const initialise = () => {
      const query = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
      if (query.get("auth_error") && sessionStatus) sessionStatus.textContent = query.get("auth_error");
      globalThis.HaraIdentity?.refresh?.().then(renderCentral).catch(() => renderCentral(null));
      refreshWorld().catch(() => renderWorld({ authenticated: false, configured: false }));
    };
    document.addEventListener("astro:page-load", initialise);
    if (document.readyState === "loading") document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", initialise, { once: true });
    else initialise();
  </script>

  <style>
    .account-stack { display: grid; gap: 1.25rem; }
    .account-panel { padding: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.75rem); border: 1px solid var(--hara-line); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--hara-surface) 84%, transparent); }
    .profile-form { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
    .profile-form label { display: grid; gap: .45rem; color: var(--hara-text); font-weight: 620; }
    .profile-form input, .profile-form textarea { width: 100%; padding: .75rem .8rem; border: 1px solid var(--hara-line); background: var(--hara-abyss); color: var(--hara-text); font: inherit; }
    .profile-form input:focus-visible, .profile-form textarea:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--hara-signal); outline-offset: 2px; }
    .profile-form small, .form-status { color: var(--hara-text-muted); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.55; }
    .profile-form__wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    .profile-consent { grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; align-items: start; }
    .profile-consent input { width: 1rem; margin-top: .25rem; }
    .button--quiet { background: transparent; }
    @media (max-width: 720px) { .profile-form { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .profile-form__wide { grid-column: auto; } }
  </style>
</SiteLayout>
